{:edb/db-before-t 1607 :edb/db-after-t 1608 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534920 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:42:55.747Z" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186198417 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444168 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186198417 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444169 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186198664 1074 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}My\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{[\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot \\frac{16}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{5}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186198664 1074 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}My\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{[\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot \\frac{16}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{5}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534920 17592186045417 false] [17592186198665 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,4\\le y\\le 6\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186198665 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,4\\le y\\le 6}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139534920 17592186045417 false] [17592186281677 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186281677 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." 13194139534920 17592186045417 false] [17592186444155 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444170 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444155 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444171 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444155 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444172 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444155 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444173 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444155 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444174 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444155 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444155 1045 "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Plane Lamina" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444155 1046 #edb/ref 17592186444170 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444155 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444155 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050741 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444155 1053 #uuid "74cd288a-6d4e-5649-a0a3-fd1f66ef23c9" 13194139534920 1759218604541