83 #uuid "9bbfff91-ca90-559f-ae5d-5fd328a1f1e9" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444164 1080 "2\\sqrt{17}" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444164 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444164 1083 #uuid "aed2bb04-ea3b-5b55-b733-92f0f589ec24" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444165 1080 "\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{2}}" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444165 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444165 1083 #uuid "bb7abb37-0de9-58cb-8a76-9f11aa3adea3" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444166 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444157 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444166 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444158 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444166 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444161 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444166 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444163 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444166 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444165 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444166 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444166 1077 "selection" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444166 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444163 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444166 1079 #uuid "02ef48a6-5de2-5aeb-b94d-50e269438d16" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444167 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444156 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444167 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444159 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444167 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444160 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444167 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444162 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444167 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444164 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444167 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444167 1077 "selection" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444167 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444160 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444167 1079 #uuid "364a1bfa-3c03-5519-b8cb-713056748a8b" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444168 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444167 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444168 1069 "q-163606" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444168 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444168 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444168 1072 #uuid "4a051470-22b3-5741-85c9-94876b2374fa" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444168 1074 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 2=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{64}{3}+4{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}21+3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{[21y+{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(63+27-21-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot 68 \\\\  & =\\frac{34M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{34}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{34}{3}}.\n$$" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444169 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444166 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444169 1069 "q-163579" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444169 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444169 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,2\\le y\\le 5\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444169 1072 #uuid "ae31463b-0937-5dcb-a149-ee8482b71924" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444169 1074 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 3=9.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{1}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}(\\frac{64}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}21\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}[y]_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}(5-2) \\\\  & =7M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=7\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{7}.\n$$" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444170 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444173 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444170 1062 #uuid "0e7b7881-d766-59e5-9ac2-17b4c071226f" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444170 1063 #edb/ref 17592186281677 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444171 1062 #uuid "512ba0cc-ab8c-5fb2-8948-44914ec8fb98" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444171 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198665 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444172 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444174 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444172 1062 #uuid "c02d457b-f21d-50f7-b09e-291abfa68047" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444172 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198664 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444173 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444172 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444173 1062 #uuid "ce124292-03a7-514d-bbf3-a753805c4055" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444173 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444169 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444174 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444171 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444174 1062 #uuid "f1544047-bb8b-536b-b9d7-9b50cf101d4e" 13194139534920 17592186045417 true] [17592186444174 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444168 13194139534920 17592186045